  #line-at(121.58pt, 120.42pt, " Department of Mechanical Engineering, University of the District of Columbia, Washington, DC, USA ")
  #line-at(178.04pt, 132.38pt, "*Corresponding authors: E-mail addresses: jiajun.xu@udc.edu (J. Xu) ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.02pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(287.42pt, 153.32pt, "Abstract ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.02pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72pt, 170.66pt, "Air-to-air heat exchangers are vital for energy recovery and thermal management but often suffer from reduced ")
  #line-at(72pt, 183.98pt, "effectiveness, high pressure losses, and increased pumping power in conventional designs. Advances in additive ")
  #line-at(72pt, 197.3pt, "manufacturing have enabled nature-inspired geometries, such as lattice and triply periodic minimal surface (TPMS) ")
  #line-at(72pt, 210.62pt, "structures, which enhance heat transfer through complex first-order surfaces but frequently cause excessive pressure ")
  #line-at(72pt, 223.94pt, "drops. This study proposes an optimized higher-order harmonic heat-transfer surface tessellation developed through ")
  #line-at(72pt, 237.26pt, "an optimization framework integrating analytical and numerical methods. The goal is to improve the overall thermal-")
  #line-at(72pt, 250.58pt, "hydraulic performance of the heat exchanger over a range of operating conditions. Results of sensitivity analysis show ")
  #line-at(72pt, 263.9pt, "that secondary surface modification of this type can yield significant increase in the effectiveness reaching up to 70% ")
  #line-at(72pt, 277.22pt, "although with associated increase in the pressure drop. The secondary surface wave frequency was found to be a more ")
  #line-at(72pt, 290.54pt, "important control parameter than the amplitude in achieving high thermal-hydraulic performance. Additionally, we ")
  #line-at(72pt, 303.86pt, "show that the optimized second order harmonic-type structure achieved relatively higher effectiveness and lower ")
  #line-at(72pt, 317.3pt, "pressure-drop than the gyroid structure in the turbulent flow regime for ")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 10.02pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(374.08pt, 317.3pt, "𝑅𝑒≥7000")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.02pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(420.82pt, 317.3pt, ". Although the gyroid TPMS ")
  #line-at(72pt, 330.74pt, "structure had relatively higher effectiveness in the laminar and weakly turbulent flow regime, the associated pressure ")
  #line-at(72pt, 344.06pt, "drop was found to be significantly higher than that of the harmonic-type structure. While the gyroid structure had ")
  #line-at(72pt, 357.38pt, "significantly higher heat transfer efficiency with an average Nusselt number about 5.2 times that the harmonic-type ")
  #line-at(72pt, 370.7pt, "structure, the corresponding flow resistance was likewise observed to be significantly higher on average, about 8.4 ")
  #line-at(72pt, 384.02pt, "times higher in the laminar flow regime and about 1.87 times higher in the turbulent flow regime. The London area ")
  #line-at(72pt, 397.34pt, "goodness factor (AGF) was used to assess the overall thermal-hydraulic performance of both architectures which ")
  #line-at(72pt, 410.8pt, "showed that the harmonic-type structure performed better in the laminar flow regime (")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 10.02pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(430.78pt, 410.8pt, "𝑅𝑒≤2000")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.02pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(477.52pt, 410.8pt, ") which had an ")
  #line-at(72pt, 424.24pt, "average AGF of about 1.72 times the AGF of the gyroid structure and reaching up 2.18 times the gyroid’s AGF when ")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 10.02pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72pt, 437.68pt, "𝑅𝑒= 500")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.02pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(113.24pt, 437.68pt, ". However, the gyroid structure outperformed the harmonic-type structure in the turbulent flow regime. The ")
  #line-at(72pt, 451.18pt, "findings from this study demonstrate a balanced pathway for additively manufacturable, high-performance air-to-air ")
  #line-at(72pt, 464.5pt, "heat exchangers, offering compact, energy-efficient solutions for applications in building ventilation, aerospace, and ")
  #line-at(72pt, 477.82pt, "electronics cooling. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.02pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(278.84pt, 499.12pt, "Introduction ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.02pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72pt, 516.46pt, "An air-to-air heat exchanger (AAHX) is a specialized device engineered to facilitate the transfer of thermal energy ")
  #line-at(72pt, 529.66pt, "between two separate air streams without permitting them to mix. This separation is critical in maintaining air quality ")
  #line-at(72pt, 542.86pt, "and preventing cross-contamination, especially in environments where hygiene and air purity are paramount [1]. The ")
  #line-at(72pt, 556.12pt, "design and development of air-to-air heat exchangers have evolved considerably over the years, leading to significant ")
  #line-at(72pt, 569.32pt, "improvements in both performance and versatility. Modern AAHX development is commonly formulated as a coupled ")
  #line-at(72pt, 582.52pt, "thermo-hydraulic optimization problem to maximize heat transfer while constraining pressure drop (Δp), size, and ")
  #line-at(72pt, 595.78pt, "manufacturability. Kim et al. (2022) expanded on such methodologies when exploring compact cross-/counter-flow ")
  #line-at(72pt, 608.98pt, "energy recovery ventilator (ERV) optimization methodologies [2]. Non-traditional core geometries to expand the ")
  #line-at(72pt, 622.24pt, "achievable heat transfer-pressure drop tradeoff have also been explored in parallel, including multi-morphological ")
  #line-at(72pt, 635.44pt, "TPMS-based microchannel concepts aimed at thermal performance optimization [3]. ")
  #line-at(72pt, 656.68pt, "The gyroid lattice structure is a complex, three-dimensional structure characterized by continuous, periodic, and non-")
  #line-at(72pt, 669.88pt, "self-intersecting channels. They have become popular due to being able to contain a large surface area within a small ")
  #line-at(72pt, 683.14pt, "volume and can be described with few geometric parameters.  Bartlett et al. (2024) describes TPMS geometries as ")
  #line-at(72pt, 696.36pt, "periodic minimal surfaces that split space into intertwined, non-intersecting channels, which gives high surface-area-")
  #line-at(72pt, 709.56pt, "to-volume ratio and avoids the sharp edges found in many compact-fin designs [4]. These designs are especially ")
]

// arXiv source page 2
#original-page(612pt, 792pt, none)[
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.02pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72pt, 81.36pt, "effective in addressing the limitations of traditional heat exchanger surfaces, which often suffer from low surface area ")
  #line-at(72pt, 94.56pt, "and inefficient heat transfer [5, 6]. By enabling increased surface contact between the air streams and the exchanger ")
  #line-at(72pt, 107.82pt, "walls, TPMS geometries significantly enhance thermal performance. Building on this, Tang, Chen, and Zhao (2024) ")
  #line-at(72pt, 121.02pt, "show that gradient and field-synergy-based optimization strategies can further improve performance by reshaping ")
  #line-at(72pt, 134.3pt, "local flow-thermal-gradient alignment to increase heat transfer at a given flow penalty [7]. ")
  #line-at(72pt, 155.48pt, "Gyroid structures offer a balance between mechanical strength and fluid dynamics, making it suitable for a wide range ")
  #line-at(72pt, 168.74pt, "of applications. However, the benefits of these advanced geometries are most pronounced under single-phase airflow ")
  #line-at(72pt, 181.94pt, "conditions. In relation, Hao et al. (2023) developed convective heat transfer correlations for TPMS-based heat ")
  #line-at(72pt, 195.2pt, "exchangers, formalizing Reynolds number (Re) and Nusselt number (Nu) relationships across representative TPMS ")
  #line-at(72pt, 208.4pt, "families to support performance prediction and design space exploration [8]. When dealing with multiphase or ")
  #line-at(72pt, 221.6pt, "turbulent flows, the performance gains may diminish due to complex interactions between the air streams and the ")
  #line-at(72pt, 234.86pt, "surface topology.  Chen, Luo, and Wei (2024) expands that TPMS-induced secondary flows and inter-channel ")
  #line-at(72pt, 248.06pt, "interactions can increase Δp and alter mixing behavior in ways that reduce net performance gains outside targeted ")
  #line-at(72pt, 261.32pt, "operating envelopes, particularly as flow regimes and transport mechanisms change [9]. ")
  #line-at(72pt, 282.5pt, "Beyond thermal-hydraulic performance, TPMS cores are attractive for lightweighting and multifunctionality because ")
  #line-at(72pt, 295.76pt, "the same periodic architecture can be co-optimized for stiffness, mass, and heat transfer, aligning with broader trends ")
  #line-at(72pt, 308.96pt, "in aerospace/transport heat exchanger lightweight design. Liu et al. (2024) discusses how these benefits are ")
  #line-at(72pt, 322.16pt, "increasingly pursued through additive manufacturing (AM), which enables fabrication of complex gyroid/TPMS ")
  #line-at(72pt, 335.42pt, "lattices and two-fluid exchange topologies that are difficult or impossible to produce conventionally [10].")
  #line-at(512.62pt, 335.42pt, "Careri, ")
  #line-at(72pt, 348.62pt, "Zocca, and Baldini (2023) emphasize the value of AM-enabled compactness and mass reduction for heat exchanger ")
  #line-at(72pt, 361.88pt, "applications [11], while Meyer et al. (2025) further highlight the performance leverage available through deliberate ")
  #line-at(72pt, 375.08pt, "internal-structure design in additively manufactured heat exchangers [12].  ")
  #line-at(72pt, 396.32pt, "Manufacturing these intricate structures presents several challenges. Practical concerns include holding tight ")
  #line-at(72pt, 409.52pt, "dimensions, limiting unwanted porosity, keeping the two air circuits leak-tight, and understanding how as-built ")
  #line-at(72pt, 422.8pt, "roughness changes friction and heat transfer. Feng, Xu, and Liu (2024) address some of these issues through ")
  #line-at(72pt, 436pt, "hierarchical TPMS lattice designs and optimization strategies that consider performance and structure together [13]. ")
  #line-at(72pt, 449.2pt, "Additive manufacturing techniques, such as selective laser sintering or stereolithography, have shown promise in ")
  #line-at(72pt, 462.46pt, "fabricating these geometries, but scalability and cost remain barriers to widespread adoption. From an optimization ")
  #line-at(72pt, 475.66pt, "standpoint, Kobayashi et al. (2021) reinforce the idea that manufacturability constraints need to be built into the ")
  #line-at(72pt, 488.92pt, "topology design process for two-fluid heat exchange, not treated as an afterthought [14]. In addition, Nazir et al. (2019) ")
  #line-at(72pt, 502.12pt, "summarize the broader state of cellular-structure additive manufacturing, noting recurring challenges with ")
  #line-at(72pt, 515.32pt, "repeatability, defect control, and cost-effective scaling [15].  ")
  #line-at(72pt, 536.56pt, "Despite the progress made in geometric optimization, most existing research on heat exchangers tends to focus on a ")
  #line-at(72pt, 549.76pt, "single operational parameter. Simulations often assume steady-state or laminar airflow conditions, which simplifies ")
  #line-at(72pt, 563.02pt, "the analysis but fails to capture the complexities of real-world environments.")
  #line-at(376.66pt, 563.02pt, "Waters (2023) explains how optimization ")
  #line-at(72pt, 576.22pt, "and additive manufacturing can produce highly efficient three-dimensional surface structures, but the broader ")
  #line-at(72pt, 589.48pt, "literature still commonly relies on steady-state and/or laminar-flow assumptions to simplify the analysis [16].  In ")
  #line-at(72pt, 602.68pt, "practice, airflow is rarely uniform; it fluctuates due to changes in occupancy, equipment usage, and external weather ")
  #line-at(72pt, 615.88pt, "conditions. These dynamic factors introduce turbulence, pressure variations, and temperature gradients that can ")
  #line-at(72pt, 629.14pt, "significantly impact heat exchanger performance.  ")
  #line-at(72pt, 650.38pt, "Because of this, gains reported under idealized simulations do not always translate into the same benefit in practice. ")
  #line-at(72pt, 663.58pt, "One clear real-world complication is flow imbalance and maldistribution. Kaminski et al. (2024) specifically compare ")
  #line-at(72pt, 676.78pt, "counterflow air-to-air heat exchangers under unbalanced flow conditions and show that off-design operation can ")
  #line-at(72pt, 690.06pt, "noticeably change heat transfer efficiency relative to balanced, uniform assumptions [17]. Such results reinforce why ")
  #line-at(72pt, 703.26pt, "simplified performance metrics can be misleading, and why more realistic modeling is increasingly important. ")
]

// arXiv source page 3
#original-page(612pt, 792pt, (image("graphics/page-03.png", width: 22.5pt), 372pt, 446.5pt))[
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.02pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72pt, 81.36pt, "To address these limitations, there is a growing opportunity for research to move beyond geometric modifications and ")
  #line-at(72pt, 94.56pt, "explore alternative strategies for enhancing heat exchanger functionality. For example, Liu et al. (2023) combines ")
  #line-at(72pt, 107.82pt, "numerical and experimental work on additively manufactured TPMS heat exchangers and demonstrate that the thermal ")
  #line-at(72pt, 121.02pt, "and hydraulic response is strongly tied to geometry, manufacturing condition, and operations, highlighting the need to ")
  #line-at(72pt, 134.3pt, "validate predicted results beyond idealized assumptions [18]. These include the use of advanced materials with tailored ")
  #line-at(72pt, 147.5pt, "thermal properties, integration of active control systems, and development of hybrid configurations that combine ")
  #line-at(72pt, 160.7pt, "multiple heat transfer mechanisms [19]. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.02pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#ee0000"))
  #line-at(233.3pt, 160.7pt, "Additionally, machine learning and artificial intelligence can be leveraged to ")
  #line-at(72pt, 173.96pt, "analyze large datasets and identify optimal design parameters under varying conditions. Guo, Lin, and Zheng (2024) ")
  #line-at(72pt, 187.16pt, "use machine learning to design and optimize staggered fin structures, showing how data-driven models can speed up ")
  #line-at(72pt, 200.42pt, "optimization and help identify robust parameter choices across broader conditions than a single simulation process ")
  #line-at(72pt, 213.62pt, "might cover [20].")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.02pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72pt, 234.86pt, "In response to these gaps, this study introduces a novel approach to heat exchanger design through the development ")
  #line-at(72pt, 248.18pt, "of an optimized, higher-order harmonic heat transfer surface tessellation. This innovative geometry is generated using ")
  #line-at(72pt, 261.5pt, "a multi-objective optimization framework that combines analytical modeling with numerical simulations. The ")
  #line-at(72pt, 274.82pt, "framework considers multiple performance metrics, including thermal efficiency, flow resistance, manufacturability, ")
  #line-at(72pt, 288.14pt, "and structural integrity. By balancing these objectives, the resulting design offers improved heat transfer capabilities ")
  #line-at(72pt, 301.46pt, "while minimizing pressure drop and material usage. The proposed tessellation is specifically tailored for air-to-air ")
  #line-at(72pt, 314.78pt, "applications, where maintaining airflow continuity and minimizing energy loss are critical. Its harmonic structure ")
  #line-at(72pt, 328.1pt, "promotes uniform distribution of air across the surface, reducing hotspots and enhancing overall thermal performance. ")
  #line-at(72pt, 341.42pt, "Furthermore, the design is compatible with modern manufacturing techniques, enabling scalable production and ")
  #line-at(72pt, 354.74pt, "integration into existing HVAC systems [21].  ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.02pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(277.94pt, 376.04pt, "Methodology ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.02pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
