#original-page(612pt, 792pt, (image("graphics/page-15.png", width: 457.5pt), 80pt, 280.5pt))[
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.02pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72pt, 81.36pt, "troughs of the primary surface of the tessellated wavy channel HX structure irrespective of the Reynolds number. ")
  #line-at(72pt, 94.68pt, "Away from the channel walls, the velocity distribution is observed to be nearly uniform. On the contrary, the velocity ")
  #line-at(72pt, 108pt, "distribution within the gyroid flow domain is characterized by regions of flow acceleration and deceleration due to the ")
  #line-at(72pt, 121.32pt, "tortuous flow-path that creates stagnation zones. Overall, the distribution of the average velocity in the gyroid unit ")
  #line-at(72pt, 134.78pt, "cell fluctuates over a wider range, e.g. from 0 to ")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 10.02pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(268.28pt, 134.78pt, "34.1 𝑚𝑠")
  #line-at(297.2pt, 134.36pt, "⁄")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.02pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(307.52pt, 134.78pt, " for ")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 10.02pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(324.52pt, 134.78pt, "𝑅𝑒= 10,000")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.02pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(378.82pt, 134.78pt, ", which is about 1.7 times more than the ")
  #line-at(72pt, 148.22pt, "value observed in the tessellated wavy channel structure. While the associated vorticity tensor magnitude also ")
  #line-at(72pt, 161.54pt, "increases with increasing Reynolds number, it is however observed to be more uniformly distributed within the flow ")
  #line-at(72pt, 174.86pt, "domain of the gyroid unit cell compared to the tessellated wavy channel structure where it is seen to be dominant ")
  #line-at(72pt, 188.18pt, "closer to the channel walls. Despite the gyroid unit cell having relatively higher velocities due to the tortuosity of the ")
  #line-at(72pt, 201.5pt, "flow-path, interestingly, the distribution of the vorticity magnitude is seen to be relatively lower, for instance, ")
  #line-at(72pt, 214.94pt, "approximately 2.25 times less than that observed in the tessellated wavy channel HX counterpart for ")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 10.02pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(483.28pt, 214.94pt, "𝑅𝑒= 10,000")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.02pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(537.6pt, 214.94pt, ". ")
  #line-at(72pt, 228.44pt, "This can be attributed to the high degree of surface undulations that characterize the channel walls of the tessellated ")
  #line-at(72pt, 241.76pt, "structure which induces local vortices near the channel walls that promote increased level of convective heat transfer ")
  #line-at(72pt, 255.08pt, "between the wall and fluid. These secondary flows may thin or disrupt the thermal boundary layer to enhance fluid ")
  #line-at(72pt, 268.4pt, "mixing. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.02pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
