  #line-at(72pt, 156.5pt, "results from the complicated and highly convoluted flow-path and its overall performance is subject to interpretation. ")
  #line-at(72pt, 169.82pt, "With the continuous advancement and growth of additive manufacturing technology, heat transfer enhancement via ")
  #line-at(72pt, 183.14pt, "surface modification with unique features can be achieved with comparable HX effectiveness as TPMS structures and ")
  #line-at(72pt, 196.46pt, "without necessarily incurring high degree of pressure drop. The optimization of second-order harmonic type heat ")
  #line-at(72pt, 209.9pt, "transfer surfaces investigated in this work as a proof-of-concept design has revealed higher AGF or ")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 10.02pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(467.62pt, 209.9pt, "𝑗𝑓")
  #line-at(471.4pt, 209.48pt, "⁄")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.02pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(482.74pt, 209.9pt, " in the laminar ")
  #line-at(72pt, 223.34pt, "flow region with reasonable HX effectiveness, however the structure loses its advantage in the turbulent flow regime. ")
  #line-at(72pt, 236.66pt, "Yet the research reveals opportunities for utilization of exotic surface equations other than that investigated in this ")
  #line-at(72pt, 249.98pt, "work for design specific and fit for purpose application. Other design factors such as fouling, design feasibility, ")
  #line-at(72pt, 263.3pt, "manufacturing cost, serviceability, etc. would ideally be taken into account for a more comprehensive and broader ")
  #line-at(72pt, 276.62pt, "scale assessment of the overall design advantage.  ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.02pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(282.08pt, 297.98pt, "Conclusion ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.02pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72pt, 315.26pt, "In conclusion, the current research has successfully investigated the performance of a heat exchanger unit cell having ")
  #line-at(72pt, 328.58pt, "heat transfer surfaces described by second-order harmonic type tessellations, in comparison to a geometrical and ")
  #line-at(72pt, 341.9pt, "hydraulically equivalent gyroid TPMS unit cell. The comparison is made on the basis of several performance metrics ")
  #line-at(72pt, 355.22pt, "including the effectiveness, pressure-drop, heat transfer efficiency, flow resistance, and overall thermal-hydraulic ")
  #line-at(72pt, 368.54pt, "performance.  ")
  #line-at(72pt, 389.9pt, "Preliminary sensitivity studies that investigate the unique contribution of the secondary surface features to the heat ")
  #line-at(72pt, 403.22pt, "exchangers performance were carried out by varying the secondary surface control parameters. It was observed that ")
  #line-at(72pt, 416.68pt, "the heat exchangers effectiveness increased at a rate of ")
